<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92744" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοώδης</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with a strong stream,
				running violently</i>, of a sea <i>in which there are strong
				currents</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				366a25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μάλιστα ῥ. τοῦ πελάγους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					7.24
				</span></i>
			: hence, of rocks, promontories, etc., <i>exposed to such
				seas</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρημνός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					8.5.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					14.24
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόποι ῥ</span>. regions <i>of
				rapid currents</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				621a16
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				3.3.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Medic.,
				<i>running</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφθαλμίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					1.5
				</span></i>
			: of persons, <i>affected with diarrhoea</i> or <i>other
				fluxes</i>, Id.<i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ὑπέρλευκοι -έστεραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					2.111
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. νόσος</span> ibid. (but
			metaph. in <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.698
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.428
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρετοὶ ῥ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρετὸς ῥ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.399
			</span></i>. Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοωδῶς πυρέσσειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cass.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					70
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> as Methodic
			t.t., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥ. νόσημα</span>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεγνόν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>Sect.Intr.</u>
				6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.29
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				2.45
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>falling off</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρπός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>CP</u>
					5.9.10
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
